<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa Gallagher dips after results.</title>
<headline>S.Africa Gallagher dips after results.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in South African firm Gallagher Ltd dipped on Tuesday after the firm posted year results still in the red, though the figures were better than last time.</p>
<p>The firm's stock dropped 26 cents to 100 cents by 0735 GMT.  </p>
<p>&quot;It is taking a hit from the figures,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Gallagher earlier posted a headline loss per share of 64 cents, against a loss of 355 cents last time. The attributable loss per share was 332 cents against 355 cents.</p>
<p>The firm paid no dividend.</p>
<p>The company also said it was overgeared at present and the board was looking at ways of reducing this. This could include a further rights offer during the current year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
